+# Incident brief, August–September 2026
+
+Status as of the 30 September on-call meeting.
+
+## 11 August: ingest stall and full disk
+
+**Impact:** Overnight, incoming data stopped for about 2.5 hours; customers saw out-of-date dashboards. The database server also filled its disk, briefly refusing writes. No data was lost.
+
+**Root cause:** One malformed batch jammed ingestion, which retried it endlessly; the retry logs filled the disk.
+
+**Fix:** Restarted ingestion with the bad batch set aside, then cleaned the database and compressed old logs.
+
+**Follow-ups:**
+- Disk alert at 80 percent (Sunil): done.
+- Stop bad batches jamming ingestion (Jonas): open, in review.
+- Unanswered pages escalate after 15 minutes (Elif, Sunil): done.
+
+## 21 September: expired API certificate
+
+**Impact:** The public API was unreachable for 47 minutes; nearly all customer connections failed.
+
+**Root cause:** The API's security certificate expired; its automatic renewal had been failing silently all month on an outdated credential.
+
+**Fix:** Renewed the certificate and restarted the API; renewal failures now raise an alert.
+
+**Follow-ups:**
+- Reminder 14 days before expiry (Priya): done.
+- Alert on days left (Priya): open.
+- Certificate check in weekly checklist (Tomasz): open.
+- Responders record steps during incidents (Mara): done.
